Description: Nodes for geostatistics in a trama graph: declaring a regionalised
    variable with coordinates, projection and boundary; exploratory spatial
    display; classical and robust empirical variograms, omnidirectional or
    directional, with large-scale trend removed; fitting spherical, exponential,
    Gaussian and Matern models by ordinary and weighted least squares or REML,
    reporting nugget, partial sill, range and practical range; and ordinary and
    simple kriging onto a boundary-clipped grid, carrying the kriging variance so
    the prediction map always has an uncertainty map beside it. The point object
    carries its coordinates, projection and boundary, so no later node asks for
    them again. Builds on trama.data for tables and trama.view for plots.
